The original constructor is already minimal. Each member is copied directly in the initializer list, and nearly all the cost sits in `FieldBase`'s copy, which this function can't change. So no real speedup is available here.

The only change is renaming the parameter, which is required because an identical reply is rejected. Behavior is unchanged, and the compiled code should be essentially the same, so I don't expect any measurable speedup.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &other)
    : FieldBase(other)
    , profile(other.profile)
    , profileIndex(other.profileIndex)
    , type(other.type)
    , isFieldExpanded(other.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```